    "summary": "Strong acoustic opener, fiery Viola Lee Blues and extended Good Lovin' jam",
    "blurb": "The Capitol Theater show opens with a punchy Casey Jones and delivers a standout Viola Lee Blues and Turn On Your Lovelight. The second half builds into an electric marathon highlighted by a soaring Good Lovin' → Not Fade Away sequence.",
    "review": "Port Chester’s March 20, 1970 concert captures the Dead in top form as they transition from an energetic acoustic set into a hard‑charging electric second set. Early songs like Casey Jones and the China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider pairing kick off the night with crisp interplay, while Pigpen’s rousing Lovelight rap adds extra fire. The highlight is undoubtedly Viola Lee Blues – a blistering blues romp that showcases Jerry’s searing lead work and the dual‑drum thunder of Mickey and Billy. That momentum carries straight into an expansive Good Lovin' → Not Fade Away jam, where the band stretches out with tight rhythmic lock‑ups and soaring solos before closing the night on a soulful Turn On Your Lovelight. Though the soundboard source has some tape hiss and Pigpen’s organ sits low in the mix, the overall performance is solid and memorable for any early‑70s Deadhead.",
